{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/879149-how-would-you-use-the-slender-man-in-the-cod","id":879149,"title":"How Would You Use The Slender Man In The CoD?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-30T18:24:13-07:00","id":879149,"title":"How Would You Use The Slender Man In The CoD?","content":"For a Chronicle centered around mortals or Hunters, Slendy could be a Horror or G-M Angel. Speaking conceptually, he could also be a True Fae, but the mechanics for them in 2ED haven't been revealed. I went into more detail about this on posts #24 and #29 of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\"><b>this thread</b></a>. <br /> <br /> Regardless of which supernatural type you choose for him, a big part of why he became so popular is the sheer mystery. Whatever modus operandi and powers he adopts in your story, there should a sense of incomprehensibility, as <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=q2duevcUMGw\" target=\"_blank\"><b>this short film brilliantly demonstrates.</b></a> You might say that picking a creature type for him is counter-productive and largely removes the Lovecraftian dread. I can see where you're coming from. However, I do not know how to properly address this issue in narrative terms. In mechanical terms, I believe the finished version of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/826279-simplified-ephemeral-being-rules-you-ll-probably-hate-this\"><b>Amechra's Revised Ephemeral Being Rules</b></a> will handle this nicely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T19:34:46-07:00","id":879185,"title":"","content":"apparently, I've made a <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/417984-carnival-of-freaks-simple-template-factory?p=431140#post431140\">template </a>half based around it a long time ago","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T11:13:34-07:00","id":883040,"title":"","content":"Hmm, well, lots of options.<br /> <br /> He could be a Thing Man Wasn't Meant to Know from Second Sight.<br /> <br /> A True Fae.<br /> <br /> A Beast.<br /> <br /> An astral entity, whatever they're called in second edition, I forget.<br /> <br /> He could be an odd form of Infrastructure","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T11:58:31-07:00","id":883079,"title":"","content":"He could straight up not exist.<br /> <br /> Oh, the characters <i>believe</i> that he's real. That much is certain. If you indulge in some... creative... scene setting, the players might believe it too (that he's real in context of the game. Don't be silly.)<br /> <br /> Hell, revealing that the &quot;terrifying&quot; &quot;supernatural&quot; being that's been chasing them is just one big elaborate gaslighting attempt? That its been a conspiracy to lead them to believe that there are secrets hidden in the shadows?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T12:19:13-07:00","id":883097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/879149-how-would-you-use-the-slender-man-in-the-cod?p=883079#post883079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hell, revealing that the &amp;quot;terrifying&amp;quot; &amp;quot;supernatural&amp;quot; being that's been chasing them is just one big elaborate gaslighting attempt? That its been a conspiracy to lead them to believe that there are secrets hidden in the shadows?</div> </div> </div> </div> Or to use their belief to bring it into being.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T13:20:38-07:00","id":883162,"title":"","content":"<i>The Author closed his notebook and slipped it into the chest pocket of the gray pinstripe suit that was part of the disguise they had decided to use for this project, then he smiled at the two warlocks across the room. &quot;Well, no, I did not manage to banish the Slender Man before you got here, rather in point of fact I could not have, it isn't real.&quot;<br /> &quot;What do you mean it isn't real? We have several witnesses and resonance from it, we even have video of it.&quot; Mercy, one of the least peaceful warlocks in the city, queried as she took a step to move around the table, obviously trying to get a clear approach in case she needed it. &quot;Do you mean it is something else? Some other sort of manifestation taking on the shape of this legend?&quot;<br /> The Author chuckled and shrugged, absent-mindedly dusting off his jacket. &quot;Well, from a certain point of view I guess that might fit, honestly though what I meant was that it couldn't be banished because it wasn't real <b>yet</b>.&quot; and then, with just a moments focus, he brought his creation into existence and told it to kill.</i><br /> <br /> Sometimes I get bored... so I make things up... :P<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","name":"Asaram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1734_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"331"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T14:05:59-07:00","id":883190,"title":"","content":"I'd... Be a Git and Make several different Entities all working together as the &quot;Slenderman&quot; A Beast for the irrational fears and paranoia that occurs with some of the Characters, Magi for the random mysteries that are crafted to drive those seeking them out Mad, A Wolfblooded/Uratha for dragging people across the veil and leaving them for Spirits.<br /> <br /> The Beast Casts the Initial feelings and Drives them towards looking for the Mystery of the being, The Mage gives them abit of the clues and the Wolfblooded/Uratha Hunts them as Prey and Drags them away.<br /> Mostly would work as a Plot for awhile to get these people into positions of Power... then i'd have something new Made because of the Fear and the like that they have caused. (Maybe even have them flee to different states/cities to get away from it.. only to have the Memetic Entity infect more people)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T14:16:48-07:00","id":883197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4MXYC_jX2Wc\" data-code=\"4MXYC_jX2Wc\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/4MXYC_jX2Wc/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> He's coming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T16:05:18-07:00","id":883275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/879149-how-would-you-use-the-slender-man-in-the-cod?p=883079#post883079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He could straight up not exist.<br /> <br /> Oh, the characters <i>believe</i> that he's real. That much is certain. If you indulge in some... creative... scene setting, the players might believe it too (that he's real in context of the game. Don't be silly.)<br /> <br /> Hell, revealing that the &quot;terrifying&quot; &quot;supernatural&quot; being that's been chasing them is just one big elaborate gaslighting attempt? That its been a conspiracy to lead them to believe that there are secrets hidden in the shadows?</div> </div> </div> </div> That's certainly a novel way to do it. I would try to put my own spin on things as well, but I can't think of anything elaborate right now.<br /> <br /> As a side note, I often imagined that Splendorman is just Slenderman when he's in a good mood.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T17:21:55-07:00","id":883328,"title":"","content":"Given the lack of proper motivations displayed beyond the apparent need to be spooky, Slenderman is easily characterized as an Horror.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T19:01:00-07:00","id":883383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/879149-how-would-you-use-the-slender-man-in-the-cod?p=883328#post883328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given the lack of proper motivations displayed beyond the apparent need to be spooky, Slenderman is easily characterized as an Horror.</div> </div> </div> </div> Very true. The only difficulty would be to limit his abilities and powers to a more manageable level. If you tried to cramp all the powers he displays in the most popular video series and blogs, he'd have over a dozen. Which powers would you say are more important for him? I'd say Surprise Entrance, Chameleon Horror, Numen (Hallucination), Eye Spy and Reality Stutter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T20:41:32-07:00","id":883438,"title":"","content":"Apart from a Horror, Slender Man could be a lot of things depending on the game line.<br /> <br /> Vampire - A Nosferatu with high Blood Potency and low Humanity. He loves children; they're delicious.<br /> <br /> Werewolf - A spirit of fear, specifically the fear of a stranger who comes take your children. Whenever people hear of a missing child, many can't help but think, <i>What if that were my child? Could it happen to me?</i>--and the Slender Man feeds on the essence.<br /> <br /> Mage - An abyssal entity. Or perhaps someone whose spell went hideously wrong.<br /> <br /> Changeling - An Exile, trying to buy its way back into Arcadia by providing captives to other Gentry.<br /> <br /> Promethean - Someone tried to create a Promethean. They failed, and instead they created <i>something else</i>.<br /> <br /> Deviant - THEY tried to turn you into something like that. Now they have a working prototype, and they're sending it after you. (Yeah I know we can't use it for a long time, and this version would probably be a Horror anyway. The idea just came to me.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/233-daydreamer","name":"Daydreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T20:59:49-07:00","id":883451,"title":"","content":"I don't know much about the Slender Man beyond two movies I saw about it, but it seems very powerful and capricious. I could easily see it being an idigam taken with the idea of urban legends and modern scary stories, particularly movies, which seem to have been a major influence in the creation of it.<br /> <br /> Though obviously it could be a wide variety of things and as Ephsy said it's pretty much what the Horror rules were made for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T21:06:30-07:00","id":883459,"title":"","content":"What would I imagine it as? My first reflex is a simple astral entity, playing off the Tulpa Effect origin.<br /> <br /> My second reflex is that it's been subjected to terrible occult stresses, due to its real vs fictional nature, worsened by the fact that half the people feeding the Tulpa believe it to be an independent creature. A lack of disciplined input and the dissonance of its ?true?false?real?impossible? status have created just enough metaphysical sympathy with the Abyss to empower it beyond the astral (and now I'm not sure if the idea of Slendy as a sock puppet for the Abyss is <i>more </i>or <i>less </i>frightening).<br /> <br /> I probably wouldn't do it that way myself in-game, though; Sleepers Accidentally Divide Urban Legend By Zero falls too flat in my mind and cleaves too closely to RL for such an iconic creature with so much story potential.<br /> <br /> ...Although the idea of mages puzzling out (most of) its origin, going in guns blazing to discorporate the threat, then discovering that the Abyssal part of Slenderman reacts <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><i>very very differently</i></span> to mages than it does to children <i>does </i>makes me giggle manically.<br /> (Spoiler: it has no eyes because it doesn't <i>need </i>eyes most of the time; kidnapping is just satisfying its imperative &quot;Be Slenderman&quot;. But mages? Oh, it <i>wants to see YOU</i>. Somehow. You're pretty sure featureless front-to-back skull-bores don't count as eyes, but whatever.)<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: I'm kind of surprised there haven't been any ghost, Geist, or underworld origins yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1289,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","user":"Hastur00","date":". 05-06-2016, 12:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T21:53:50-07:00","id":883483,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/343572-angelic-glitches\">A glitchy angel.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T22:09:03-07:00","id":883488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/879149-how-would-you-use-the-slender-man-in-the-cod?p=883483#post883483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/343572-angelic-glitches\">A glitchy angel.</a></div> </div> </div> </div> I first heard the idea of Angel!Slendy on Reddit, but it was your post that made me realize he'd have to be a very unusual one. After some searching, I found out that Korogra came up with <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/246019-primer-corrupted-programs-aberrations-of-the-god-machine\"><b>Aberrants</b></a>, which do sound more like Slendy than a typical Exile. Satchel has a point about Angelic Covers being very sturdy.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T22:14:06-07:00","id":883490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hastur00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/879149-how-would-you-use-the-slender-man-in-the-cod?p=883459#post883459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would I imagine it as? My first reflex is a simple astral entity, playing off the Tulpa Effect origin.<br /> <br /> My second reflex is that it's been subjected to terrible occult stresses, due to its real vs fictional nature, worsened by the fact that half the people feeding the Tulpa believe it to be an independent creature. A lack of disciplined input and the dissonance of its ?true?false?real?impossible? status have created just enough metaphysical sympathy with the Abyss to empower it beyond the astral (and now I'm not sure if the idea of Slendy as a sock puppet for the Abyss is <i>more </i>or <i>less </i>frightening).<br /> <br /> I probably wouldn't do it that way myself in-game, though; Sleepers Accidentally Divide Urban Legend By Zero falls too flat in my mind and cleaves too closely to RL for such an iconic creature with so much story potential.<br /> <br /> ...Although the idea of mages puzzling out (most of) its origin, going in guns blazing to discorporate the threat, then discovering that the Abyssal part of Slenderman reacts <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><i>very very differently</i></span> to mages than it does to children <i>does </i>makes me giggle manically.<br /> (Spoiler: it has no eyes because it doesn't <i>need </i>eyes most of the time; kidnapping is just satisfying its imperative &quot;Be Slenderman&quot;. But mages? Oh, it <i>wants to see YOU</i>. Somehow. You're pretty sure featureless front-to-back skull-bores don't count as eyes, but whatever.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: I'm kind of surprised there haven't been any ghost, Geist, or underworld origins yet.</div> </div> </div> </div> I do believe any mages that try to investigate Slendy should have a real &quot;oh shit&quot; moment, rather than going &quot;meh, it's just a Goetia&quot; or whatever.<br /> <br /> I agree that ghostly origins could be very interesting. The implications of a Geist version would be very different from a Cthonian one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T19:34:41-07:00","id":884262,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1289_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1289\" data-vbnamecard=\"1289\">Hastur00</a>: Like you said, Slendy is more of an idea than a creature. That's a pretty accurate description of most Goetia. However, the way people keep changing how they think about him, and the attempts by some occultists to bring him into reality via Tulpa Effect could result in infection by the Abyss.<br /> <br /> As for a ghostly version, I always thought he had a very patriarchal air, and not just because of the suit. I've heard that he sometimes returns children when they apologize for misbehaving, but what he might consider reprehensible is nebulous. I've also heard that many people he stalks as adults were also stalked by him when they were children. Maybe he repeats his punishments when these people fall back on the bad behaviors of their childhoods? Is he trying to keep them from leaving behind ghosts due to unfinished business?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T05:05:59-07:00","id":884553,"title":"","content":"I ran a Halloween one shot a few years ago where slendy was actually a spirit of urban legends, and by getting turned into a meme he was defeated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T09:34:49-07:00","id":885425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/879149-how-would-you-use-the-slender-man-in-the-cod?p=884262#post884262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for a ghostly version, I always thought he had a very patriarchal air, and not just because of the suit. I've heard that he sometimes returns children when they apologize for misbehaving, but what he might consider reprehensible is nebulous. I've also heard that many people he stalks as adults were also stalked by him when they were children. Maybe he repeats his punishments when these people fall back on the bad behaviors of their childhoods? Is he trying to keep them from leaving behind ghosts due to unfinished business?</div> </div> </div> </div>I hadn't heard it let kids <i>go</i>. With that in mind, the suit, the height... yeah, patriarchal is a really interesting, solid take. Easy motive to grok, bent and fractured enough to make it even more alien and uncomfortable.<br /> <br /> In another direction, there's lore that suggests Slendy <i>never </i>stops; any child or investigator that draws its attention <i>will </i>eventually culminate in a vanishing or a death. That says ghost <i>harvesting </i>to me, although what it wants either blank slates or broken slates, I couldn't conjecture. What happens to mortals taken to a Kerberos' or Cthonian's realm if they stay?<br /> <br /> I also like playing with the idea that it exists backwards in time; it does... whatever it does to its victim, and then returns to the victim's timeline over and over, to &quot;steer&quot; them to their already inevitable end. If we take Sigma radiation as a confusion or corruption of EM forces, I'm thinking temporal Angel that didn't stop to ask directions, and glitched when it got snarled in dimensional-causal structures. Despite the fact that the gears that power its ability to utilize Covers are stripped, It's still providing a useful service, whatever that might be. So rather than bringing in an unpredictable, productive, deaf-and-dumb agent, the G-M slapped a meme on it and called it a day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T10:11:57-07:00","id":885462,"title":"","content":"You know I actually made a True Fae for the Slenderman - they called him the Faceless Man. Other names for him included Der Gross Mann (The Tall Man), Fear Dubh (The Black Man), The Clutchbone, and my personal favorite, The Erkling (The Elf King, or King of the Fairies). It was very useful to use in the chronicle for the sheer amount of lore already readily available. Honestly, it worked so perfectly I think I'd have trouble seeing him as another creature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T12:34:12-07:00","id":885586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hastur00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/879149-how-would-you-use-the-slender-man-in-the-cod?p=885425#post885425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hadn't heard it let kids <i>go</i>. With that in mind, the suit, the height... yeah, patriarchal is a really interesting, solid take. Easy motive to grok, bent and fractured enough to make it even more alien and uncomfortable.<br /> <br /> In another direction, there's lore that suggests Slendy <i>never </i>stops; any child or investigator that draws its attention <i>will </i>eventually culminate in a vanishing or a death. That says ghost <i>harvesting </i>to me, although what it wants either blank slates or broken slates, I couldn't conjecture. What happens to mortals taken to a Kerberos' or Cthonian's realm if they stay?<br /> <br /> I also like playing with the idea that it exists backwards in time; it does... whatever it does to its victim, and then returns to the victim's timeline over and over, to &quot;steer&quot; them to their already inevitable end. If we take Sigma radiation as a confusion or corruption of EM forces, I'm thinking temporal Angel that didn't stop to ask directions, and glitched when it got snarled in dimensional-causal structures. Despite the fact that the gears that power its ability to utilize Covers are stripped, It's still providing a useful service, whatever that might be. So rather than bringing in an unpredictable, productive, deaf-and-dumb agent, the G-M slapped a meme on it and called it a day.</div> </div> </div> </div> If I had to guess, someone imprisoned in a Dead Dominion would have to bargain with the Kerberos for sustenance and shelter, much like a mortal making pacts with the Wyrd to survive in Arcadia. Someone imprisoned by a Cthonian probably wouldn't have any way of bargaining, as Cthonians don't enforce any Old Laws. <br /> <br /> And if Slendy is a ghostly patriarchal figure...who or what is his wife? Are they still together? Do they have &quot;children&quot;?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T17:01:53-07:00","id":885795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/879149-how-would-you-use-the-slender-man-in-the-cod?p=885586#post885586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if Slendy is a ghostly patriarchal figure...who or what is his wife? Are they still together? Do they have &quot;children&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>The shipping community thinks so<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> ...but seriously, now all I can think of is Slendy-the-Cthonian striving mightily to assume even vaguely human form, undertaking the all but unimaginable journey back to the world of the living, to lead children on a lengthy, nightmarish trek back to its cold, unhappy Persephone so she'll forget her cold, unhappy eternity for just a little while. Whatever else it is, whether unrequited, contracted, or genuine but nearly forgotten, it has what can only be described as <i>regard </i>for another mortal Below.<br /> <br /> I can't imagine it ends well for the <i>kids, </i>though<i>.</i> Perhaps it takes them swimming from time to time.<br /> <br /> Why do I let this s**t rattle out of my mouth, I made myself sad now &gt;:-C","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T11:22:03-08:00","id":1165632,"title":"","content":"OK, after a long time of thinking about this. I believe I figured out my ideal way to represent the Slender Man.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Virtue:</b> Fearsome<br /> <b>Vice:</b> Observant/Mysterious<br /> <b>Aspirations:</b> Take People Away, Stay Just Out Of Sight, Invade And Twist Lives For Unknown Reasons, + ST Fiat<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 6, Wits 6, Resolve 8<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 6, Dexterity 8, Stamina 8<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 8, Manipulation 6, Composure 10<br /> <br /> <b>Skills: </b>Academics 2, Investigation (Spying) 4, Occult 3, Medicine 1, Athletics (Chasing) 4, Brawl (Claws And Tentacles, Grappling) 3, Stealth (Stalking, In Plain Sight) 8, Survival (Forests And Woodlands), 3, Empathy (Comforting, Fear) 3, Expression (Gestures) 2, Intimidation (Appearing Out Of Nowhere, Lurking Dread) 8, Persuasion (Taking People Away) 4, Subterfuge (Evasive, Mind Games) 5<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b> Area Of Expertise 1 (Fear), Direction Sense 1 (Advanced 2, Epic 2), Eidetic Memory 2, Indomitable 2 (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/843870-advanced-merits-homebrew-collaboration\"><b>Advanced 3, Epic 4</b></a>), Interdisciplinary Specialty 1 (Fear), Trained Observer 3 (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/843870-advanced-merits-homebrew-collaboration\"><b>Advanced 2</b></a>), Vice-Ridden 2, Double Jointed 2 (Advanced 1), Greyhound 1, Seizing The Edge 2, Iron Will 2, Striking Looks 2 (Advanced 2, Uncanny Valley), Untouchable 1, Fighting Finesse 1 (Claws And Tentacles, Grappling), Killer Instinct 3 (Advanced 3)<br /> <br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 28<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 10<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 18<br /> <b>Speed:</b> ST Fiat<br /> <b>Health:</b> 17 (Size 9)<br /> <b>Potency:</b> 10<br /> <br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Claws And Tentacles [+2L Melee; 12 dice]<br /> <br /> <b>Ban 1:</b> Cannot harm children<br /> <br /> <b>Ban 2:</b> Can only go after those who have Investigated him<br /> <br /> <b>Ban 3:</b> May only use Living Legend to assume forms and gain powers in accordance with whatever would cause the most fear in its current victims (look to their Aspirations and Breaking Points for guidelines)<br /> <br /> <b>Bane:</b> No longer being a mystery (i.e. allowing its current victims to gather Clues about it equal to its Composure + Potency)<br /> <br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Chameleon Horror (Invisible Horror), Home Ground (Forests And Woodlands), Elusive, Immortal, <u><i><b>Living Legend</b></i></u>, Madness And Terror, Maze, Numen (Aggressive Meme, Hallucination, Mortal Mask, Occult Sight, Seek, Teleportation), Surprise Entrance, Vanish, Price Of Power x 4<br /> <br /> <b>Elusive: </b>Creatures with this Dread Power only ever appear on camera as a blurred silhouette of their actual shape. Humanoid monsters can easily be mistaken for humans or upright bears, while unusually large creatures blend into the scenery. Humans have a hard time remembering exact detail about creatures they encounter. Rolls to accurately describe or recall such events are made at a \u20133 modifier. By spending 1 Willpower, the Horror increases this penalty to -6 and Failures are downgraded to Dramatic Failures for one scene (a Beat is still earned).<br /> <br /> <b>Invisible Horror (Prerequisite - Chameleon Horror):</b> The Horror becomes wholly invisible. The penalty the Horror imposes upon attempts to perceive it granted by Chameleon Horror becomes -6 in all circumstances. Supernatural perceptions can pierce this Invisibility, invoking a Clash of Wills against the Horror\u2019s Composure + Potency to negate the penalty imposed by this Dread Power until the end of the scene. In addition, the Horror receives Rote Quality on Stealth rolls, and may make Stealth rolls even when moving at full Speed. In most cases Invisibility is a permanent aspect of the creature, but some can control when they are visible. In the latter case, altering its visibility for a scene costs the Horror one point of Willpower. The creature\u2019s Invisibility imposes a Ban - which is always condition where it does not apply (such as infrared light or when observed by children).<br /> <br /> <b>Living Legend: </b>The Slender Man is considered to be an ever changing entity that draws its power from the collective imagination of humanity, but is also given shape and limitations by it. Mechanically, it has the Shifting Dread Power of the Idigam, and also a number of Influence dots equal to its Potency that it may swap around with Shifting. It may also swap around Numina with Shifting.<br /> <br /> <b>Occult Sight:</b> Slender Man is sensitive to supernatural phenomena. It notices the active use of supernatural abilities within the range of its senses and may make Perception rolls to approximate their distance and direction. In addition, by spending a point of Willpower, it can see through powers of concealment, illusion and deceit with a Clash Of Wills using its Wits + Potency. Lastly, it always knows when it is being targeted by a supernatural power and may mimic the Aura Reading Supernatural Merit, but without drawback.<br /> <br /> <b>Teleportation:</b> When the entity moves, it may reflexively spend 1 Essence to vanish and reappear at another location within its line of sight up to its (Rank x Speed) in yards away. Doing so adds +2 to its Defense for the turn. If the entity has the Seek Numen, it may teleport to the nearest location with a suitable Condition by spending 3 Essence. The entity can spend an additional 2 points of Essence to take a passenger with them (an unwilling passage may resist with a roll of Resolve + Composure + Supernatural Tolerance).<br /> <br /> <b>Vanish: </b>The Horror with this Dread Power can disappear in a flash, a puff of smoke, or the blink of an eye. Once per scene, by spending 1 Willpower, the creature may instantly exit the scene. The Slender Man may also bring other people with him, but must first open all the Doors of the target. Those that Vanish with Slender Man cease to exist unless Slender Man brings them back.<br /> <br /> <b>Price Of Power:</b> By taking on an additional Ban or Bane, an entity can increase its repertoire of abilities. Each additional Ban or Bane can give it one of the following.<br /> <br /> * Two Numina, Influence dots, or Manifestations.<br /> * An increase of its maximum Essence pool by 5.<br /> * A Dread Power.<br /> <br /> An entity may take this Numina a number of times equal to its Rank.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> This part is courtesy of Pale_Crusader.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>---Side Bar---</b><br /> <b>Where are the Telepathic Powers?</b><br /> Slender Man is known for his powerful telepathic mind control. People blame Slender Man for possessing them, for mind controlling them, for forcing them to do the awful things they do in his name. The tragic truth is he has no such power other than his frightening presence and he never even makes requests. His presence is supernaturally terrifying, and having Slender Sickness disrupts normal thinking but does not rob its victims of agency. The horrible things Slender Man followers do they decide for themselves. He stalks, he lurks, he harries and terrifies but ultimately his victims do the most monstrous things all on their own.<br /> <b>----------------</b><br /> <br /> <b>SLENDER SICKNESS CONDITION</b><br /> Those with this Condition are valid targets of Slender Man's SURPRISE ENTRANCE Dread Power. Also at the beginning of each session the player of the character chooses one of the follow conditions to apply at some point during that session: Frightened, Lost, Shaken, or Spooked. The Storyteller chooses when that happens in the story with a fleeting glimpse of Slender Man. If the character doesn't have a player associated with it mechanically (meaning she isn't a PC, nor does she represent a Merit, Touchstone or similar mechanic), the Storyteller chooses the Condition.<br /> <b>Cause:</b> Those that actively investigate the truth that Slender Man exists and believe it gain this Condition. It is not enough to be told, the person with this condition has researched and earnestly sought out proof of the rumors and urban legends and found it. Mechanically this can be handled with the Clue system in CoD page 81, requiring 3 Clues (or for Mages the use of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/886930-sample-mysteries?p=1108928#post1108928\">Focused Mage Sight with a Mystery Opacity of 1</a>).<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> Gain the Amnesia Condition concerning everything they know about Slender Man (if they lose that Condition they regain this one)<br /> <b>Beat: </b>Have Slender Man use SURPRISE ENTRANCE Dread Power to enter a Scene with the character. (The other Conditions gained by this Condition grant Beats normally)<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Slender Man\u2019s Mystery Cult</span></b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Originally posted by <b>Jamie Seidel, News Corp Australia Network</b> <br /> A brutal stabbing attack by pre-teens obsessed with the Slenderman puts spotlight back on the popular culture of horror stories. HE is the abnormally tall figure who stalks children and inspired two girls to stab a classmate. What is the real story behind Slenderman? IT'S an internet horror-cult that almost caused a killing. Now the hosts of the \u201cSlenderman\u201d myth believed behind a brutal pre-teen attack have defended their art.<br /> <br /> Website creepypasta.com, which presents itself as a Wikipedia-style collection of paranormal and horror \u2018microfiction\u2019, has posted a long defence of the story it hosts that has became an internet meme \u2014 and the trigger for the vicious weekend attack.<br /> <br /> Two Milwaukee girls told investigators they plotted for months to kill their friend because a character called Slenderman required them to kill someone before they could become his &quot;proxy&quot;. Both 12-year-olds have been charged as adults for first-degree attempted homicide. </div> </div> </div>This once obscure internet subculture of creepy fiction has hit mainstream news. For those that don't delve into that subculture and investigate the urban legend as if it were real, that's as far as the story goes, a tragic story of mentally unwell little girls doing something awful. Dig deeper and things can get much, much worse. Slender Man is real, and he can invade your life and turn the rest of it into a horror story. There are many members of this cult that began as people making metafiction or creating a hoax to find out they've became active participants within a horror story.<br /> <br /> <b>Relics:</b> Recordings with Slender Man in them.<br /> <br /> <b>Doctrine:</b> The &quot;doctrine&quot; of this cult is cobbled together from paranoid delusions, insomnia hallucination, wild speculation, and internet rumor. It takes many forms from adherent to adherent, but boils down to various attempts to appease Slender Man as if he were some type of ancient evil god of old. What appeasement means varies in interpretation ranging from murder and blood ritual to spreading of the Slender Sickness. The latter is far closer to the truth than the former, but there is no way for those with the Slender Sickness to know that until they reach the deepest portion of the mystery cult.<br /> <br /> <b>Cultists:</b> Youtubers, Horror Writers, Internet Addicts, Role players using Slender Man in their games<br /> <br /> <b>Initiation Benefits</b><br /> <b>\u2022</b> All initiates learn to how to dig into urban legends in their pursuit of Slender Man. They gain a Investigation Specialty in Urban Legends.<br /> <b>\u2022\u2022</b> Full members hone their skills at uncovering hidden truths. They gain the Investigative Prodigy 1 Merit free of charge.<br /> <b>\u2022\u2022\u2022</b> As a cultist delves into the mysteries of Slender Man, she gains insight into the doom such research represents, whether that is madness, a gruesome death, or actually being taken by Slender Man. She gains the Cursed 2 Merit, and it is at this point they gain the Slender Sickness Condition (Slender Man doesn't have this Condition, obviously).<br /> <b>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</b> The fervor of those that know this much is contagious. They gain a variant of Inspiring 3 Merit that instead gives Obsession (Slender Man) Condition instead.<br /> <b>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</b> Those that know the ultimate secret of Slender Man can fabricate Clues (CoD page 80) to the Slender Man mystery which act as the contagion for Slender Sickness. Slender Man himself has this ability but can only use it by mystically and retroactively inserting real Clues into staged hoax footage. For those with Slender Sickness the creation of Clues is a way to placate Slender Man.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}